{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87085b39155089f1","type":"tool_result","content":"# OSUM-EChat: Enhancing End-to-End Empathetic Spoken Chatbot via Understanding-Driven Spoken Dialogue\narXiv: 2508.09600\nAuthors: Xuelong Geng, Qijie Shao, Hongfei Xue, Shuiyuan Wang, Hanke Xie, Zhao Guo, Yi Zhao, Guojian Li, Wenjie Tian, Chengyou Wang, Zhixian Zhao, Kangxiang Xia, Ziyu Zhang, Zhennan Lin, Tianlun Zuo, Mingchen Shao, Yuang Cao, Guobin Ma, Longhao Li, Yuhang Dai, Dehui Gao, Dake Guo, Lei Xie\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We introduce OSUM-EChat, an end-to-end empathetic spoken dialogue model that effectively perceives paralinguistic cues and generates contextually aligned empathetic responses.\n  2. We present an understanding-driven spoken dialogue training strategy and a linguistic-paralinguistic dual think mechanism to transfer knowledge from speech understanding to dialogue generation in resource-limited settings.\n  3. We introduce the EChat-200K dataset and EChat-eval benchmark to provide a rich paralinguistic speech-to-speech dialogue corpus and a comprehensive multi-dimensional empathy evaluation framework.\n  4. We provide a complete open-source ecosystem including the model, codebases, datasets, and data construction workflows to foster community-driven empathetic dialogue research.\n\nTags: LALM/对话型-交错标记, LALM/理解型, LALM/训练-指令微调\n===\nPaper 2502.04424 not found","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db7dfc54-061a-477c-b9b4-ce921795d299","uuid":"dbdb2602-a1e7-45f0-8f55-1fa59288a496","timestamp":"2026-08-11T11:47:19.566Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# OSUM-EChat: Enhancing End-to-End Empathetic Spoken Chatbot via Understanding-Driven Spoken Dialogue\narXiv: 2508.09600\nAuthors: Xuelong Geng, Qijie Shao, Hongfei Xue, Shuiyuan Wang, Hanke Xie, Zhao Guo, Yi Zhao, Guojian Li, Wenjie Tian, Chengyou Wang, Zhixian Zhao, Kangxiang Xia, Ziy